{"title":"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb17c1bc295194d9f50e1be9517bb7786bae42a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\dfrac{6^2-1}{6^2+11}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{7^2-2}{7^2+12}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{8^2-3}{8^2+13}\\right)\\cdots\\left(\\dfrac{2012^2-2007}{2012^2+2017}\\right)=\\dfrac{m}{n},\\]\" width=\"471\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive relatively prime integers, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad681354a2a529a1828a56b2b5629faec3cd128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> be a recursion defined such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60d3af914e46132967036c2eb502a14bc544cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=1, a_2=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/429152f22012c318ab1c4745ff61e6d79b38dbc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\sqrt{\\left| a_{n-1}^2-a_{n-2}^2 \\right|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"164\" height=\"32\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be91d8532fe2a50e227f2fec7c3cecdd8758df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e943dc9ba74c0dd51eaeac23d962253885a233ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> being a positive integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> being a positive integer greater than 2, find the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a78a9191f622742b577956b12b98c88016e25b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96674b050996130f384e636a6a0f329ea756a21d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{digital root}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> of a number is defined as the result obtained by repeatedly adding the digits of the number until a single digit remains. For example, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96674b050996130f384e636a6a0f329ea756a21d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{digital root}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df47bd6423e18bb7a0275cc3ebb3e91c5fc72455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$237$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b0810abe1ee69b36a84ca5103ae509f73ada088f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2+3+7=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877005097846a15901d8f294dde6e6076615a3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2=3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. Find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96674b050996130f384e636a6a0f329ea756a21d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{digital root}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797e3604b6c641ef9fad3ad33ed92c2a351c9121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012^{2012^{2012}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be a triangle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822b800ca9993bd5686e4fe3a128c4659d3e979d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f8fcfe896fcde9d2732076f4f3c3a94cf78f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784f7f7f7228d0a77323715dca18f50aee49eb8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be the points where the angle bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectfully, intersect the sides opposite them.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f023e647e33b8ceceae24114f49af3e0daa7780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI_B=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3dc5f886983b13d1ebde19d56691e46586ee591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI_B=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524357c7c05ca81cb99795978ae1ef533c19889e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI_A=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />, then the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5c8184b908a7ec8b5f7e744d496fb83908ed37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI_C:BI_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive relatively prime integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A fair die with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sides numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive is rolled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> times. The probability that the sum of the rolls is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48f95ec89b6c50220ecbbbb6130586135db8ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is nonzero and is equivalent to the probability that a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is rolled. Find the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and center in the first quadrant is placed so that it is tangent to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis.  If the line passing through the origin that is tangent to the circle has slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4a7df1100efe353cc612d5d1c289c22d5bf8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of the center of the circle can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf6c57e9a33f99ae6a5daf92e3ba24c86a621a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m+\\sqrt{n}}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"66\" height=\"42\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a61870035304b46bdbcafc39d04bea20e3899c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> are positive real numbers that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcdf6153cc81d8ffe189f7743591977c31986788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+4y+1=3\\sqrt{x}+2\\sqrt{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />, then the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 7\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a point outside circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that the tangents from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3793743e5c9b274fe5cce88f179734f74dce4205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAO=15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> first intersect the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and extend the parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to meet the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3dea44afdfb1750c0b0667f04148664ff376ca82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC^2=m+k\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2c2d940b225be2cb344eddb55d6cc720d2778f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 8\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd17cd296404d0c6d0a3c231fdb77597e9e9348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f07beb633addcca15137a3dd14227b2ac740dd42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=20$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7342d63bab2d6492dc1e197535d8d0ccee0eb2d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdcf886dffa6d211e37d5856d9c264431f641725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}, \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, respectively.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f26b7a33460dbb48fc22896c98b458f0762aae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\frac{1}{4}AB, BF=\\frac{1}{4}BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"197\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b848202c5dfa90a3ade215599b58e620543aeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=\\frac{1}{4}AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"37\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5cf3bc943044a0ab0d7c2cb43401a37bdf7aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}-c\\sqrt{d}}{e}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"44\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cbe98d2864aae78c25b55b49ae5482c8a50e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d, e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> are all positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> do not have any perfect squares greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as divisors.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e9da7691c4a59208721a2da0f7bbc510d639fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 9\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a set of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4cb295fb5e3c46c5c50f7081389fd31cf879a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{lucky}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> if it can be split into two nonempty disjoint subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382cea990fadd43376cf42e8e0597a5eb13a67c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d22cf9cc08f3cc7d6e30883a2410c58ff5bccf91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\cup B=S$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> such that the product of the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and the product of the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382cea990fadd43376cf42e8e0597a5eb13a67c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> sum up to the cardinality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Find the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4cb295fb5e3c46c5c50f7081389fd31cf879a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{lucky}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> sets such that the largest element is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. (Disjoint subsets have no elements in common, and the cardinality of a set is the number of elements in the set.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 10\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There exist real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e42302f9dd0afe4a7cd50ac2115f72bee849423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e1c555b3e8a580935c559e891dd775da1cadd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e1076cafecb0bbfe9bef3f3e90a5610d8ca7503b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+b^3=3n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> for some value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e23ee5b2a6a2daad7e00cd3a21708d6f107343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^4+b^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 11\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a25e6f563be9f04bf763c1a229bf56246cf440ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a}b=5\\log_{b}ac^4=3\\log_{c}a^2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"21\" />. Assume the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e53879a6763708feecf1f63879b9c161f0c398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> has three real solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fde197a47bfe41d98f14a8c1e09244961a85cca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{z}=-\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"142\" height=\"40\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 12\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Regular octahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> (such that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are coplanar and form the vertices of a square) is divided along plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, parallel to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, into two polyhedra of equal volume. The cosine of the acute angle plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> makes with plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5208d7e26a727fb86ed2f4b83db6a10a76becc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=30$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, find the area of the cross section made by plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with octahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 13\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a number a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf26ccc758c80896260a7e5049b30949b0b4cd33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{near Carmichael number}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"180\" height=\"12\" /> if for all prime divisors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf26ccc758c80896260a7e5049b30949b0b4cd33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{near Carmichael number}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"180\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d76bd4a232f2d7216a6cd53196e566f1e086eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/7955459cf8b75c3ac12c23c393024177d7d56412.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not prime. Find the sum of all two digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9d4336cf33c125a5c9ef6f93bb0b7fc791fed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{near Carmichael numbers}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"186\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 14\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e978a0825dc57184086cbb00ed2da1875cf3a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"101\" height=\"48\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/9238d82d59d5dfe79e96d916bfdf2f4acc4ed3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b19d463d56a72694a86ad5305d8888fd255b8ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2+1, a_3+8, a_4+27, a_5+64, a_6+125, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"363\" height=\"16\" /> is an arithmetic sequence, find the smallest positive integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191d57d1e5f185fb30c1bc518df495e0b7d7bbf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&lt;-2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 15\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141127\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 814/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27235/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10972:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017141127 and revision id 148959. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}